---
import Container from "@components/Container.astro";
import PageLayout from "@layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import Link from "@components/Link.astro";

import { SITE, SOCIALS } from "@consts";

const USES = {
  TITLE: "Uses",
  DESCRIPTION: "A living index of the physical hardware, everyday carry, digital tools, and self-hosted infrastructure I use to stay functional, focused, and calm.",
};
---

<PageLayout title={USES.TITLE} description={USES.DESCRIPTION}>
  <Container>
    <div class="space-y-16">
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h1 class="animate font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">
          Tools, tech, and gear I use daily.
        </h1>
        <article class="space-y-4 text-black/75 dark:text-white/75">
          <p class="animate">
            As a creative designer with an AuDHD brain, my setup isn't built around performative aesthetic minimalism or hoarding tactical survival gadgets. It is engineered around friction reduction: eliminating cognitive dropouts, protecting auditory bandwidth, offloading working memory to physical paper, and keeping my digital environment entirely autonomous.
          </p>
          <p class="animate">
            This is a living inventory of the hardware, carry, and software stack that keeps my day from going into the weeds.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <!-- 01. The Split Key System -->
      <section class="animate space-y-4">
        <h5 class="font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">
          01. On-Body Carry & The Split Key Rig
        </h5>
        <article class="space-y-3 text-black/75 dark:text-white/75">
          <p>
            Keys are universally the first casualty of an absent mind. I split my keys into two dedicated functional modules to keep them lightweight, silent, and purpose-built:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Car Key Module:</strong> Paired with a <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">VAFOTON 240W Short USB-C Cable (21cm)</strong> on the ring. It bends double on itself into a clean fob loop, providing an instant 240W PD charging tether without loose cable spaghetti in my pockets.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">House Key Module:</strong> Tamed inside an <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Orbitkey Key Organiser</strong> to kill the maddening jingle on long walks. It carries a <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">SanDisk Ultra Dual Drive Go (128GB)</strong>—partitioned into a bootable Ventoy rescue layer and an air-gapped terminal dashboard—and a spring-loaded <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Resqme Car Escape Tool</strong>.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>

      <!-- 02. Sensory & Memory -->
      <section class="animate space-y-4">
        <h5 class="font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">
          02. Sensory Protection & Working Memory
        </h5>
        <article class="space-y-3 text-black/75 dark:text-white/75">
          <p>
            Managing sensory noise and working memory dropouts isn't optional; it is baseline cognitive maintenance.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Google Pixel Buds Pro:</strong> Active noise cancellation acts as acoustic body armour against supermarket refrigeration hums, cafe chatter, and traffic rumble.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Loop Quiet 2 Earplugs:</strong> Kept clipped to my bag's zip pull inside their carry case. Passive silicone attenuation that never runs out of charge when an environment gets aggressive.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Field Notes (Kraft Dot-Grid 3.5" x 5.5"):</strong> Paper has zero notification badges to hijack my dopamine loop. Essential for rapid wireframes, scratchpad logic, and fleeting tasks.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Uni Jetstream 4&1 Multi-Pen:</strong> Houses four smooth hybrid ink colours, an integrated 0.5mm mechanical pencil, and an eraser in a single body.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Matador Waterproof Pill Canister:</strong> Machined aluminium capsule holding an afternoon stimulant dose and emergency analgesics.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Heavy Tactile Worry Coin & Microfibre Cloth:</strong> Silent kinetic grounding for long conversations, and clean glass to kill visual micro-irritations before they cause subconscious fatigue.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>

      <!-- 03. The Utility Pouch -->
      <section class="animate space-y-4">
        <h5 class="font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">
          03. The Utility Rig (Daily Hardware)
        </h5>
        <article class="space-y-3 text-black/75 dark:text-white/75">
          <p>
            Instead of loose tools rattling at the bottom of a pack, my mechanical gear lives indexed inside a compact fabric magazine pouch with an elastic side loop:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Olight Pro Torch:</strong> High-output dedicated beam for unlit boots and hunting behind server racks without torching phone battery.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Swann-Morton Retractable Scalpel:</strong> Surgical-grade British retractable handle for opening deliveries and precision scoring.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">B-2 Probe by STLTH:</strong> Sits in the pouch's elastic loop. A micro-probe for fiddly manipulation, prying open tight electronics tabs, and scraping labels.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Mr. Green Ultra-Thin Travel Nail Clippers:</strong> Folds wafer-flat to kill rough nail edges before they hijack hyperfocus.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Anker Nano Power Bank:</strong> Slots straight into the base of my phone via an integrated connector without trailing wires.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">The Pack:</strong> <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Bellroy Lite Sling Mini</strong> or <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Alpaka Go Sling Nano</strong> with a light-coloured interior lining. When unzipped, every piece of gear is visible in one second.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>

      <!-- 04. Digital Workspace -->
      <section class="animate space-y-4">
        <h5 class="font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">
          04. Digital Workspace & Terminal
        </h5>
        <article class="space-y-3 text-black/75 dark:text-white/75">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Windows Terminal & PowerShell 7:</strong> GPU-accelerated tabbed terminal runner handling modern pipeline operations, paired with the <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Starship</strong> cross-shell prompt for real-time Git status.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Typography:</strong> <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">JetBrains Mono Nerd Font</strong> for terminal ligature support and developer glyphs; <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Inter</strong> for calm desktop UI reading.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Obsidian & Git:</strong> Local-first, markdown-based digital garden for architecture, notes, and technical documentation.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Inkscape:</strong> Standalone open-source vector graphics workhorse for branding, layouts, and SVG wireframes.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>

      <!-- 05. Security & Cloud -->
      <section class="animate space-y-4">
        <h5 class="font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">
          05. Security, Cloud & Network
        </h5>
        <article class="space-y-3 text-black/75 dark:text-white/75">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Proton Suite:</strong> Proton Mail and Proton Drive for primary zero-knowledge communications and encrypted daily cloud storage.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">KeePassXC:</strong> Local, encrypted <code class="text-xs bg-black/5 dark:bg-white/10 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">.kdbx</code> password vaults stored offline on physical media.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Proton VPN:</strong> Standalone WireGuard profiles exported directly for encrypted network tunnels across desktop, mobile, and live Linux sessions.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>

      <!-- 06. Homelab -->
      <section class="animate space-y-4">
        <h5 class="font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">
          06. Homelab & Infrastructure
        </h5>
        <article class="space-y-3 text-black/75 dark:text-white/75">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Proxmox VE:</strong> Running bare-metal on dedicated compact x86 nodes, hosting lightweight LXC containers and isolated virtual machines.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Home Assistant:</strong> Local-first smart home telemetry, energy monitoring, and automated hardware control without vendor cloud dependencies.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-black dark:text-white">Edge Connectivity:</strong> Cloudflare Zero Trust tunnels and local DNS fallbacks.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>

      <!-- Social Footer Links -->
      <section class="animate space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-black/10 dark:border-white/10">
        <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          {SOCIALS.map(SOCIAL => (
            <li class="flex gap-x-2 text-nowrap">
              <Link href={SOCIAL.HREF} external aria-label={`${SITE.NAME} on ${SOCIAL.NAME}`}>
                {SOCIAL.NAME}
              </Link>
              {"/"}
            </li>
          ))}
          <li class="line-clamp-1">
            <Link href={`mailto:${SITE.EMAIL}`} aria-label={`Email ${SITE.NAME}`}>
              {SITE.EMAIL}
            </Link>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </Container>
</PageLayout>